<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mahdist State</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1874–1898 (in Darfur)</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Mahdist interregnum, Mahdist</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mahdist State was the state founded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sudan">Sudan</a> by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ahmad">Muhammad Ahmad</a>, who proclaimed himself the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahdi">Mahdi</a> in 1881, and continued under his successor the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abdallahi-ibn-muhammad">Khalifa Abdallahi</a>. Following al-Zubayr's defeat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darfur-sultanate">Darfur</a> sultan in 1874, Darfur was absorbed by the Mahdists, extinguishing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/keira-dynasty">Keira</a> authority. The site refers to the period from 1874 to 1898 in Darfur as the Mahdist interregnum.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mahdist-state.jpg" alt="Mahdist State" width="320" height="267" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Samhanin · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Mahdi_movement_in_Sudan.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
